        reason: `\`stop_reason\` is the authoritative, structured signal the API provides for loop control. Continuing on \`"tool_use"\` and terminating on \`"end_turn"\` is the correct pattern — it uses the model's own structured output rather than fragile natural language parsing. Checking for "task complete" text is an anti-pattern: the model may phrase completion differently, include the phrase mid-task, or never include it at all. Option A (arbitrary iteration cap) is a secondary safety measure, not a primary termination mechanism. Option C (absence of tool calls) is unreliable — \`end_turn\` without tool calls is the correct signal, not the absence of tool calls per se. Option D adds unnecessary infrastructure when \`stop_reason\` already provides the required signal.`,
