        reason: `Claude Code is designed to be interruptible at any point using Escape. For irreversible actions like file deletion during a complex task, the correct pattern is to pause, clarify, and make an explicit decision before proceeding. Option A delegates an irreversible decision entirely to Claude without verification. Option C accepts unnecessary risk — restoring from version control adds friction and assumes the broader task completed correctly. Option D — switching to plan mode mid-execution — is not a supported recovery mechanism for in-flight actions.`,
